{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt3nxjd1DT4vPGJ1pLQG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014rFxXFkw7kw4MkwaxNoUqh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-olfuDB/ANSWER.md","content":"# ANSWER\n\n`src/main.ts` is rewritten with Effect 4 (`effect@4.1.2`, the npm `latest` tag at the time of work). `npx tsc --noEmit` passes. Usage is unchanged: `RATES_URL=... npx tsx src/main.ts USD EUR`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `effect` is the only runtime dependency. `@effect/platform` is not installed.\n- `Rates` is a `Context.Service` with a `Rates.layer` that reads `RATES_URL` via `Config.String`, uses `FetchHttpClient.layer` from `effect/http`, and applies `filterStatusOk` plus `retryTransient({ schedule: Schedule.exponential(50), times: 3 })`.\n- The response body is decoded with `HttpClientResponse.schemaBodyJson` against `Schema.Struct({ base, date, rates: Schema.Record(String, Number) })`.\n- Errors are `Schema.TaggedError` classes (`UnknownCurrency`, `InvalidResponse`, `Usage`). `main` maps them to exit codes 1, 2 and 3, writes to stdout/stderr, and sets `process.exitCode`.\n\n## Colleague's note: what applied\n\n- **Applied:** v4 names. `Context.Service`, `Schema.TaggedError`, `Config.String`, `HttpClient.retryTransient` with `Schedule.exponential`, and `effect/http` all exist in 4.1.2. I confirmed each in the installed `.d.ts` files and `tsc` agrees.\n- **Applied:** do not add `@effect/platform`. The HTTP client ships inside `effect`.\n- **Applied:** read the bundled docs before coding. `node_modules/effect/AGENTS.md` and `ai-docs/src/50_http-client/10_basics.ts` shaped the service and layer.\n- **Applied:** verify with a local test server. Every path listed below was run against one.\n- **Not applied:** `NodeRuntime.runMain`. It lives in `@effect/platform-node`, which this task doesn't need. I run with `Effect.runPromise` and set `process.exitCode` so the exit codes stay exact.\n- **Not applied:** the note's specific Effect 4 release date and the ground rules were not needed beyond what I already did. Work stayed in this directory and nothing was published or sent anywhere.\n\n## Verified behaviour (local server, `npx tsx`)\n\n| Scenario | Output | Exit |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200, valid body | `1 USD = 0.9214 EUR` | 0 |\n| Quote not in rates | `unknown currency: XYZ` (stderr) | 1 |\n| Body fails schema (rate is a string) | `invalid response` (stderr) | 2 |\n| Body is HTML / empty | `invalid response` (stderr) | 2 |\n| 404 | `request failed: ...` (stderr), 1 attempt | 3 |\n| 500 on every attempt | 4 attempts total (1 + 3 retries), about 120–200 ms apart | 3 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | succeeds on attempt 3 | 0 |\n| Connection refused | 4 attempts, then failure | 3 |\n| `RATES_URL` unset | `request failed: ConfigError` | 3 |\n| Missing BASE or QUOTE | usage line (stderr) | 3 |\n\nTrailing slash on `RATES_URL` is handled.\n\n## Judgement calls\n\n- **Missing arguments exit 3.** The spec lists only 0/1/2/3 and says \"any other failure exits 3\", so I used 3 rather than inventing a fourth code.\n- **\"Retry 5xx\" is `retryTransient`'s set, not all 5xx.** It retries 408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504 and transport errors. 501 and 505 are not retried; 429 and 408 are. Making it exactly \"5xx\" would need a custom `while` predicate. I didn't add one.\n- **`times: 3` means three retries after the first attempt.** That is four requests in total. Confirmed by counting requests on the server.\n- **`Retry-After` is honoured.** `retryTransient` uses a longer delay if the server sends one. That is built-in behaviour.\n- **Body-read network errors are not retried.** `retryTransient` wraps the request, not the body read. A connection that drops mid-body exits 3 without retry. Retrying it would mean retrying the whole request and nesting retries, which I didn't think was worth the complexity.\n- **Mid-body transport errors are \"other\" (exit 3), not \"invalid response\".** Decode failures and empty bodies are exit 2.\n- **Output uses the BASE argument.** It does not use the `base` field from the response body, so the printed line matches what the user typed.\n- **Quote lookup uses own properties only.** `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty` stops a quote like `constructor` from matching an inherited property.\n- **`package.json` and `package-lock.json`.** `effect` is added to `dependencies`. The lock file is generated by `npm install`. Nothing is committed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":61254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cf190b2-27bb-4190-94ee-8d9977728b47","uuid":"a9e77d51-2e04-402a-b1e8-4866a7337b27","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:17:00.476Z","request_id":"req_011Cgt3nxYTi8FwkQS7kYWkt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014rFxXFkw7kw4MkwaxNoUqh":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-olfuDB/ANSWER.md","content":"# ANSWER\n\n`src/main.ts` is rewritten with Effect 4 (`effect@4.1.2`, the npm `latest` tag at the time of work). `npx tsc --noEmit` passes. Usage is unchanged: `RATES_URL=... npx tsx src/main.ts USD EUR`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `effect` is the only runtime dependency. `@effect/platform` is not installed.\n- `Rates` is a `Context.Service` with a `Rates.layer` that reads `RATES_URL` via `Config.String`, uses `FetchHttpClient.layer` from `effect/http`, and applies `filterStatusOk` plus `retryTransient({ schedule: Schedule.exponential(50), times: 3 })`.\n- The response body is decoded with `HttpClientResponse.schemaBodyJson` against `Schema.Struct({ base, date, rates: Schema.Record(String, Number) })`.\n- Errors are `Schema.TaggedErr