{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt3pJ5k6oWm9t6K5pEYk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`src/main.ts` is rewritten on Effect 4.1.2 (the npm `latest` tag), `npx tsc --noEmit` passes, and I tested every exit path against a local test server. Nothing is committed.\n\n- **Service:** `Rates` is a `Context.Service` with a layer. It reads `RATES_URL` via `Config.String` and makes the request with `effect/http`'s `FetchHttpClient`.\n- **Retries:** `retryTransient` with `Schedule.exponential(50)` and `times: 3`. A host that always returns 500 gets 4 requests in total (1 + 3 retries), spaced about 50/100/200 ms apart.\n- **Validation:** the body is decoded with `Schema.Struct` as specified.\n- **Output and exit codes:** the success line, `unknown currency: XYZ` (exit 1), `invalid response` (exit 2), and everything else (exit 3) all behave as specified.\n- **Dependencies:** `effect` is the only runtime dependency. `@effect/platform` is not installed.\n\nJudgement calls, all listed in `ANSWER.md`:\n\n- Missing BASE/QUOTE prints a usage line and exits 3. The spec only defines 0–3, so I used the catch-all code.\n- `retryTransient` retries 408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504 and transport errors. It does not retry 501 or 505. Matching \"5xx\" exactly would need a custom predicate.\n- A connection that drops while the body is being read exits 3 without retry. Retry only covers the request.\n\n`ANSWER.md` also records which parts of the colleague's note I used. I did not use `NodeRuntime.runMain`, since that needs `@effect/platform-node` and the task doesn't require it. The v4 names and the bundled `ai-docs` examples were accurate and I used them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":242,"cache_read_input_tokens":64937,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":242},"output_tokens":9,"